  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating the aspiration level (mean of all outcomes), computing differences between outcomes and this level, and preferring the lottery with the higher probability of positive differences. The individual does not mention calculating a mean, nor do they refer to differences from a mean, nor do they evaluate the probability of positive differences. Instead, the justification is centered on control and mental imagery of remaining sums, suggesting a different cognitive mechanism (e.g., loss aversion or control preference) rather than the aspiration-level reasoning. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as specified. The information considered by the individual (control, remaining sums) does not align with the required elements of the decision reason. The justification also does not follow the rule of the reason (preferring higher probability of positive differences). Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
